From be56f4ea27b76902a537cc238ad58485e664d67c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex contributors <codex@invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 01:43:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(wayland): negotiate normal colour descriptions with one
 owner

Use exact protocol-v2 compound power or supported v1 extended-sRGB/linear
encodings for ordinary GTK rendering. Handle v2 ready/preferred events and
retain live descriptions with bounded opaque identity tokens, preserving
the existing target SDK layout and native lease contract.

Require an advertised pass-through Vulkan format when GTK can manage the
native Wayland surface, while retaining the no-manager legacy path.
Prepare native wire regressions against the actual private producer.

The unchanged four-object compiler prerequisite passed before these edits.
Candidate compilation, test execution and runtime qualification remain held.
